{"title":"2021 Fall AMC 12A Problems/Problem 19","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Easy_Solution_with_Intermediate_Value_Theorem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Easy Solution with Intermediate Value Theorem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Mathematical_Dexterity\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Mathematical Dexterity</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_TheBeautyofMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_MRENTHUSIASM_(English-Chinese_Bilingual)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by MRENTHUSIASM (English-Chinese Bilingual)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> be the least real number greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/1/371c380ac7b9ad377bc6804e3a912eb76719946c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin(x)= \\sin(x^2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"127\" height=\"21\" />, where the arguments are in degrees. What is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> rounded up to the closest integer?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/c/f8caa073c5c4d48a79802235ab16051a74a2fd1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } 10 \\qquad \\textbf{(B) } 13 \\qquad \\textbf{(C) } 14 \\qquad \\textbf{(D) } 19 \\qquad \\textbf{(E) } 20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"401\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The smallest <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> to make <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/4/e9480229ab9813f3cd2d9526576f269352587cc2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin(x) = \\sin(x^2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"127\" height=\"21\" /> would require <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/a/65a5f453d95b58cf37ac6705ef455d129545d2af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=x^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"54\" height=\"17\" />, but since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> needs to be greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, these solutions are not valid.\n</p><p>The next smallest <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> would require <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/6/1964b99834363a381dad4f46ebeaddbd7f32a8f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=180-x^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"104\" height=\"18\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/a/aaa16385025899a979797ca8e5f0053bda68d060.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2+x=180$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"104\" height=\"18\" />. \n</p><p>After a bit of guessing and checking, we find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/0/1704b626a6dd74d07aeec2bc8b65c7faae065af7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12^2+12=156$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"119\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/d/82de2ae7a6aa2d6adba23900675f52b3657eca28.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13^2+13=182$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"119\" height=\"18\" />, so the solution lies between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/3/cd366188e09c264a7578018e08ad979a928eb7cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12{ }$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/0/030e19e4e2f1c074127cb50581e8496470c5419f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, making our answer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/1/0015d81ecedfa82ac18a09fab1897cbc9e176f9e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) } 13}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"71\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>Note: One can also solve the quadratic and estimate the radical.\n</p><p>Note: the answer is 13 because 182 is far more close to 180 than 156 and as x is positive then it is much closer, so the answer is 13\n</p><p>Note: solving: x^2+x-180=0 so x= (-1+- sqrt(721))/2 clearly only x= (-1+sqrt(721))/2 is feasible here. we make a rough estimate of 721 being 729 (as 729 is the closet perfect square),  so it is (-1+27)/2=13.    in addition, we could try to estimate with 12 (which is the worth case),   26^2=4*169 =676 which yeilds us x=(-1+26)/2=12.5 which closely, it is still 13 (12.5 is close to 13) \n</p><p>therefore the answer is undeinablely 13. majorly it is some addition onto the original basis\n</p><p>~kingofpineapplz and edition by chundoowan\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For choice <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/3/cb3db983b534373488fba3fdfaf7b692194bb301.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"33\" height=\"17\" /> we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/5/d85cf0503e8abddc34dd48d55e87735b286320c5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\left| \\sin x - \\sin \\left( x^2 \\right) \\right| &amp; = \\left| \\sin 10^\\circ - \\sin \\left( \\left( 10^2 \\right)^\\circ \\right) \\right| \\\\ &amp; = \\left| \\sin 10^\\circ - \\sin 100^\\circ \\right| \\\\ &amp; = \\left| \\sin 10^\\circ - \\sin 80^\\circ \\right| \\\\ &amp; = \\sin 80^\\circ - \\sin 10^\\circ . \\end{align*}\" width=\"330\" height=\"103\" />\nFor choice <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/d/a5d19752c57bc1e73b61c9b9940635a708e80943.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(B)},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"35\" height=\"18\" /> we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/f/b9f004402d304ec3d04de0025faa0340ee139c4b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\left| \\sin x - \\sin \\left( x^2 \\right) \\right| &amp; = \\left| \\sin 13^\\circ - \\sin \\left( \\left( 13^2 \\right)^\\circ \\right) \\right| \\\\ &amp; = \\left| \\sin 13^\\circ - \\sin 169^\\circ \\right| \\\\ &amp; = \\left| \\sin 10^\\circ - \\sin 11^\\circ \\right| \\\\ &amp; = \\sin 11^\\circ - \\sin 10^\\circ . \\end{align*}\" width=\"330\" height=\"103\" />\nFor choice <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/0/3e0177d15168f7b1af172ddb1ebd4ae8d56b1aea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(C)},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"17\" /> we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/3/6a3c2d384d4647fe645ec2df16103fc6e06f08e7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\left| \\sin x - \\sin \\left( x^2 \\right) \\right| &amp; = \\left| \\sin 14^\\circ - \\sin \\left( \\left( 14^2 \\right)^\\circ \\right) \\right| \\\\ &amp; = \\left| \\sin 14^\\circ - \\sin 196^\\circ \\right| \\\\ &amp; = \\left| \\sin 14^\\circ + \\sin 16^\\circ \\right| \\\\ &amp; = \\sin 14^\\circ + \\sin 16^\\circ . \\end{align*}\" width=\"330\" height=\"105\" />\nFor choice <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/6/2d6d83615701ee2c7146b42a9ddaec6d734aca3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(D)},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"36\" height=\"18\" /> we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/c/f0ca02a4131f2c71ba359308fb160c61bc63b871.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\left| \\sin x - \\sin \\left( x^2 \\right) \\right| &amp; = \\left| \\sin 19^\\circ - \\sin \\left( \\left( 19^2 \\right)^\\circ \\right) \\right| \\\\ &amp; = \\left| \\sin 19^\\circ - \\sin 361^\\circ \\right| \\\\ &amp; = \\left| \\sin 19^\\circ - \\sin 1^\\circ \\right| \\\\ &amp; = \\sin 19^\\circ - \\sin 1^\\circ . \\end{align*}\" width=\"330\" height=\"103\" />\nFor choice <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/e/7ae69570c458db7421453f5388296ee0a31fb370.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(E)},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"31\" height=\"17\" /> we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/6/d665d658dce6213cf3b1112d8e41189d5f61d55c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\left| \\sin x - \\sin \\left( x^2 \\right) \\right| &amp; = \\left| \\sin 20^\\circ - \\sin \\left( \\left( 20^2 \\right)^\\circ \\right) \\right| \\\\ &amp; = \\left| \\sin 20^\\circ - \\sin 400^\\circ \\right| \\\\ &amp; = \\left| \\sin 20^\\circ - \\sin 40^\\circ \\right| \\\\ &amp; = \\sin 40^\\circ - \\sin 20^\\circ . \\end{align*}\" width=\"330\" height=\"103\" />\nTherefore, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/3/dc314329e6eee4c97892d39ba3638a6ceb1731ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) }13},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"71\" height=\"30\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/f/0cf80a3e0e22f1a2e08ee462fb126886943b4ceb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin 11^\\circ - \\sin 10^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"126\" height=\"16\" /> is the closest to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/4/604c735470dd0152ca1cff75fe26eadf5cef7f49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>~Steven Chen (www.professorchenedu.com)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Easy_Solution_with_Intermediate_Value_Theorem\">Easy Solution with Intermediate Value Theorem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Easy Solution with Intermediate Value Theorem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/3/4533b4d8a731706a2f78668fca3c513af10222d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2-x=180-2x+360k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"205\" height=\"18\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/1/9e18555d90b8930d82598f7bee89f540e51433a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2-x=360k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"114\" height=\"18\" /> from looking at the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/3/f33d76347cd543cea100642d6a37a9fed59c7527.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{sin}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"22\" height=\"13\" /> values on the unit circle. \nWith these equations, we can just insert the values that are given in the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> answers. \n</p><p><br />\nLet's try <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/4/7c43070a2acf8f4e25d98e48c404d9348a26d40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{A}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"12\" height=\"12\" /> first. \n</p><p>We know that one of the equations should be greater on the left, and another equation we make should be greater on the right for the solution to be in between the values inserted into the equations. \nThe two numbers it is in between is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> since it is rounded up. \n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/4/f24dbdab20ef9418932837f4f5ec51b0ade66c61.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100-10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"70\" height=\"15\" /> vs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/9/6790876dc1bd7ee74b1098de7d9a210b81eba58c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$180-20,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"75\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/4/51435a6f8842c9ac0f13f05bc3b1a4ad953d1b05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$81-9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"15\" /> vs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/7/0c7eac9c7329d8646b05d428de2598266b9974e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$180-18.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"75\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><br />\nThis does not satisfy what we would like to find.\n</p><p><br />\nNow let's try <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/9/09920c3af0daa12ac2ec5174e737c31e0f8cec75.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{B}$\" width=\"11\" height=\"11\" />.\n</p><p>Between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/0/030e19e4e2f1c074127cb50581e8496470c5419f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />;\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/b/8eb7a4e70d8df8feee6840cfaf67e2a01665916b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$144-12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"70\" height=\"15\" /> vs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/6/b06a04678a452b408cb0fe53e2a48124e98636c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$180-24,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"75\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/8/56883067a791ab9d41f6dc0d548d5b2483af973f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$169-13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"70\" height=\"15\" /> vs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/7/e97a949b536a4f3f3c26099467921257238a221b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$180-26.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"75\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><br />\nNow this satisfies our hunt for the solution.\nThe answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/b/69bb65d8b09333c4d5a11be52f4f7df860510d21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\text{(B)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"36\" height=\"28\" />\n</p><p>emilyyunhanq@gmail.com\n</p><p>Solution by Emily Q\n</p><p><br />\n(edited by A7456321)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Mathematical_Dexterity\">Video Solution by Mathematical Dexterity</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Mathematical Dexterity\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=H0pNJFbV4jE\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=H0pNJFbV4jE</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_TheBeautyofMath\">Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Solved both Mentally and by writing things down\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/o2MAmtgBbKc\">https://youtu.be/o2MAmtgBbKc</a>\n</p><p>~IceMatrix\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_MRENTHUSIASM_.28English-Chinese_Bilingual.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_MRENTHUSIASM_(English-Chinese_Bilingual)\">Video Solution by MRENTHUSIASM (English-Chinese Bilingual)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by MRENTHUSIASM (English-Chinese Bilingual)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/n2YiM8xUTBs\">https://youtu.be/n2YiM8xUTBs</a>\n</p><p>~MRENTHUSIASM\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12A\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12A\">2021 Fall AMC 12A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Re